.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWN-PROFILES 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clown-profiles
.Nd the clown named-profile registry, profiles.toml
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clown/profiles.toml
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A named profile bundles a provider, an API backend, a model, credentials,
environment and an optional saved MCP tool selection under one name.
.Nm clown
selects one with
.Fl -profile Ar name ,
the
.Ev CLOWN_PROFILE
environment variable, a
.Xr clownfile 5
.Sy [profile]
pin, the interactive picker, or the build's default profile, in that
order; an explicit
.Fl -provider
suppresses the pin and the build default but never an explicit
.Fl -profile .
A selected profile is an explicit choice: its model and environment win
over the
.Xr clownfile 5
.Sy [profile]
defaults.
.Pp
The registry is the builtin profiles compiled into
.Nm clown
merged with the user's
.Pa profiles.toml .
A user profile with a builtin's name replaces that builtin; builtins
cannot be removed.
Each profile is validated when it is selected.
.Cm clown profile list
shows the builtins: one each for
.Cm claude ,
.Cm opencode
and
.Cm crush
with the
.Cm anthropic
and the
.Cm local
backend (there is no builtin
.Cm gateway
or
.Cm openrouter
profile), and claude worker templates
.Pq Li reviewer , Li porter , Li canary No and its variants
that keep only the MCP servers and tools their task uses and set
.Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_CLAUDEAI_CONNECTORS
and
.Ev CLOWN_DISALLOWED_TOOLS
in their
.Sy env .
.Sh FILE FORMAT
.Pa profiles.toml
is TOML: one
.Sy [[profile]]
table per profile and one
.Sy [registry]
table that
.Nm clown
writes.
.Ss [[profile]]
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy name
The profile's name, as given to
.Fl -profile .
.It Sy display
A human-readable label for the picker and
.Cm clown profile list .
.It Sy provider
One of
.Cm claude ,
.Cm opencode ,
.Cm crush
or
.Cm openrouter .
.It Sy backend
.Cm anthropic ,
.Cm gateway
or
.Cm local
for
.Cm claude ,
.Cm opencode
and
.Cm crush ;
only
.Cm gateway
for
.Cm openrouter .
.It Sy model
The model.
For the claude-family providers it is passed as
.Fl -model
unless the command line already has one.
A
.Cm claude
profile with a
.Cm gateway
or
.Cm local
backend and no
.Sy url
resolves this name through juggler's model registry; see
.Xr juggler 7 .
.It Sy url , Sy token
The gateway endpoint and its credential.
.Cm claude Ns + Ns Cm gateway
needs
.Sy url
or
.Sy model ,
and
.Sy token
whenever
.Sy url
is set;
.Cm openrouter
needs
.Sy token
(its URL is fixed);
.Cm opencode
and
.Cm crush
with
.Cm gateway
need both.
Both values expand
.Li $NAME
and
.Li ${NAME}
references, so a token can stay in the environment rather than in this
file.
.It Sy env
A table of environment variables for the provider.
A variable already set in the ambient environment wins; one set only by
the
.Xr clownfile 5
.Sy [profile.env]
table is overridden.
.It Sy context_servers
A saved
.Fl -cheap-context
selection: the exact list of MCP servers to keep, each named
.Ar plugin Ns / Ns Ar server .
Every other discovered server is stopped.
It is a keep-list, not a deny-list; there is no way to name servers to
drop.
An empty list is rejected, since it would read back as no selection at
all.
A saved server that a launch no longer discovers is skipped, but a launch
under a selection that keeps none of the running servers is refused
rather than falling back to every plugin un-narrowed.
.It Sy context_excluded
A table keyed by a kept server's
.Ar plugin Ns / Ns Ar server
name whose values are lists of that server's own tool names to hide from
the agent.
It is a deny-list only; there is no per-tool allow-list.
A key naming a server the profile does not keep is ignored.
A name matches a live tool exactly or by the claude-safe form claude
shows it under (moxy's
.Li grit.branch
is
.Li grit_branch ) .
.It Sy base
.Ar builtin
or
.Ar builtin Ns Li @sha256: Ns Ar hex :
the builtin profile this one claims to narrow, optionally pinned to that
builtin's canonical digest (64 lowercase hex digits).
Nothing is inherited from the base: it is a declaration a launcher checks.
.Nm clown
refuses a launch whose base names no builtin or whose pin no longer
matches.
Builtins themselves cannot carry a base.
.Cm clown profile edit
and the
.Fl -cheap-context
save prompt keep a profile's base as it is; neither offers to change it,
so set or change it by editing the file.
.El
.Ss [registry]
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy clown_version
The version of the
.Nm clown
that last saved the file.
.It Sy protocol
The lowest registry protocol that holds the file's profiles:
.Li 2
when any profile uses
.Sy base ,
else
.Li 1 .
.El
.Pp
Every save through
.Nm clown
writes this stamp.
A launcher that reads the registry through clown's
.Li pkg/profilelookup
library, such as spinclass, refuses a registry with no stamp, one stamped
with a protocol it does not speak, one with keys it does not know, and one
that uses
.Sy base
under a protocol older than 2.
A hand-written file therefore needs a
.Sy [registry]
table before spinclass will use it; saving any profile through
.Cm clown profile
adds one.
.Sh CHEAP-CONTEXT SELECTIONS
.Nm clown Fl -cheap-context
starts every discovered MCP server, shows a picker of servers and tool
groups, stops each fully deselected server, and hides the deselected tools
of the rest.
It needs an interactive terminal.
After the picker it offers to save the selection into a profile, new or
existing; the saved fields are
.Sy context_servers
and
.Sy context_excluded .
Saving into an existing profile replaces
.Sy context_servers
with this launch's kept servers, and the exclusions of each server the
picker showed tool by tool with what was picked for it.
A server the picker could not show tool by tool (one inside an agent unit,
one whose catalog could not be fetched, one with a single tool group, one
not started this launch) keeps its saved exclusions as they were.
A server dropped from
.Sy context_servers
is not started on replay, so exclusions saved for it then have no effect.
Launching with a profile that carries them replays the selection without
the picker.
When a selection stops a server or hides tools, a claude session's system
prompt ends with a short notice naming the profile (or the picker) and the
stopped servers, and giving each kept server's hidden-tool count; tool names
are not printed, and the notice is bounded in size.
A launch that narrows nothing gets no notice.
.Pp
Tools are hidden by a
.Li POST /clown/exclude-tools
to the server's own HTTP endpoint.
.Xr clown-stdio-bridge 1
answers it for servers a plugin declares as
.Sy stdioServers ;
a native HTTP server must implement it itself, as moxy does
(moxy#399).
Without a profile a failed push is logged and that server keeps its full
catalog.
Under a profile's saved selection each kept server's saved names are
matched against its live catalog, the matches are pushed, the catalog is
fetched again, and the launch is refused unless every match is gone from
it.
It is also refused when none of a server's saved names matches a live tool:
the tools that list meant to hide may have been renamed and now be visible.
A partly stale list is accepted, and its stale names are skipped.
It is refused, too, when a saved name could mean a live tool without
matching it exactly or matches more than one, and when the server's catalog
cannot be fetched.
Servers inside an agent unit are checked the same way by the unit, which
refuses the confined launch.
The result is recorded in
.Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/readback/ Ns Ar principal Ns Pa .json .
.Pp
A worker reports to its driver over the
.Li clown-builtin-jobs/ringmaster
and
.Li clown-builtin-jobs/troupe
servers.
A profile whose selection drops either, or excludes tools from either,
leaves a worker mute; spinclass refuses to spawn with such a profile.
.Sh SESSION PINS
When a launch applies a profile,
.Nm clown
records the profile's name and canonical digest against the session in
.Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/session-names.jsonl .
Resuming that session must apply the same profile with the same digest:
resuming under another profile, under none, or after the pinned profile's
definition changed is refused, with a short field diff that never prints
tokens, environment values or credentialed URLs.
A session with no pin takes a defaulted profile on first resume, while an
explicitly requested one needs the launcher's approval.
.Pp
A launcher approves a change by passing
.Fl -profile
together with the environment below;
.Nm clown
removes all three variables from its own environment so no child inherits
them.
This guards against operator mistakes and silent drift, not against an
agent that can set its own environment or write clown's state directory.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CLOWN_PROFILE
The profile to apply, as
.Fl -profile ;
the flag wins when both are given.
.It Ev CLOWN_PROFILE_DIGEST
The launcher's approval: the canonical sha256 digest the applied profile
must resolve to.
A launch whose profile resolves to another digest, or that applies no
profile, is refused.
.It Ev CLOWN_PROFILE_SESSION
Binds that approval to one session id; any other launch is refused.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm clown profile list
Print every merged profile with its source
.Pq Li builtin , Li user No or Li user override
and how many servers its selection keeps.
.It Cm clown profile add
.It Cm clown profile edit Ar name
Create a profile, or change an existing one, in a form.
.Cm edit
fails on a name that is not a profile; editing a builtin saves a user
override.
The form covers
.Sy name
through
.Sy token ;
.Sy env ,
.Sy context_servers
and
.Sy context_excluded
are kept as they are and can be changed only by hand or by the
.Fl -cheap-context
save prompt.
.It Cm clown profile remove Ar name
Remove a user profile after a confirmation.
.El
.Pp
.Cm add ,
.Cm edit
and
.Cm remove
need an interactive terminal and write
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clown/profiles.toml
atomically, mode 0600, keeping the file's comments and layout.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clown/profiles.toml
The user registry
.Pq Pa ~/.config/clown/profiles.toml No when Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME No is unset .
.It Pa ~/.config/juggler/profiles.toml
The legacy location, read with a warning when the canonical file does not
exist; never written.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/session-names.jsonl
Session records, including profile pins.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/readback/ Ns Ar principal Ns Pa .json
The exclusion readback of the last launch under a saved selection.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[profile]]
name = "narrow"
display = "Claude, moxy without gmail"
provider = "claude"
backend = "anthropic"
model = "claude-sonnet-5-5"
context_servers = ["moxy/moxy", "clown-builtin-jobs/ringmaster",
  "clown-builtin-jobs/troupe"]

[profile.context_excluded]
"moxy/moxy" = ["gmail_read", "gmail_triage"]

[registry]
clown_version = "0.3.20"
protocol = "1"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown 1 ,
.Xr clown-stdio-bridge 1 ,
.Xr clownfile 5 ,
.Xr juggler 7
